-- ADDED: ANIMATION CHANGER (Misc page, below the "ANIMATIONS" header)
--   Only the animation packs part of Evora was taken (EvoraHub_Christmas.lua, "ANIM PACK"): the same 23 packs (same ids,
--   same order, "Adidas Sports" first) and the same way of applying them: the ids inside the character's "Animate" script
--   (idle Animation1/Animation2, walk, run, jump, fall, climb, swim, swimidle) are replaced and the playing tracks are
--   stopped so the new ones load. A pack that has no entry for a slot (e.g. Werewolf has no jump) leaves that slot as the
--   game had it. Applied again after every respawn (0.75 s after CharacterAdded, like Evora).
--   UI: toggle "Animation Changer" (G.WaveTogglePill_Anim) and the "<  pack  >" row (G.TextButton_AnimPrev / _AnimNext).
--   Arrows: change the pack; pressing one while the toggle is OFF also turns the toggle ON.
--   Config: the toggle is stored by the generic toggle capture; the chosen pack goes through G.VisualsCtl
--           (state.visuals.animPack), so autosave / Save Config / Load / Reset Config include it. Old configs load fine.
--   Differences from Evora (on purpose):
--     * The original id of every slot is kept in an attribute ("WindOrigAnimId") on the Animation instance, so switching
--       the toggle OFF (or to another pack) puts the game's own ids back, even after the script was executed twice.
--       Evora keeps them in a table and asks Humanoid:GetAppliedDescription instead.
--     * Evora's "Harder Hit Anim" master toggle is not part of this (it is not in Wind).
--   Only works for characters that have the standard "Animate" LocalScript (R6 / R15 default). A game with its own
--   animation system prints a warning and nothing changes.
-- ==========================================================================
do
	local Players = game:GetService("Players")
